lars for britain's  healthcare workers by walking laps in  his backyard  he always had a positive attitude please  remember  tomorrow will be a good day became his  trademark motto  the 100 year old died earlier this month  after testing positive for covet 19.  this same unforgiving virus he did so  much to fight  still ahead a holocaust survivor's  decades-long search for a lost  friendship  you might want to grab a box of tissues  for tonight's episode of global's the  new reality because you'll likely fall  in love with its main character  she's a 91 year old holocaust survivor  whose story starts with a cherished bond  during 1930s nazi germany  and wraps up over eight decades later  with a zoom call  our mike armstrong has been calling it a  friendship  interrupted mike well robin this story  is incredibly unlikely and equally  unforgettable we met betty gribenshikov  in florida she grew up in berlin in the  1930s and  jewish what that meant was as she got  older she watched her freedom  stripped away year after year by the  late 1930s when betty was seven and  eight years old  jews in germany weren't allowed in parks  or on beaches  they weren't even allowed to ride  bicycles it was very  gradual the whole thing was very gradual  you know the hitler youth kids were out  there  they used to be my friends they lived  right around where we lived in the same  apartment building one day you're  playing with them  one day and the next day they call me a  dirty jew  what that meant was the friends she had  were important her best friend was a  little  girl anna marie warrenberg they did  everything together  except escape from nazi germany but he  got out with her family before the war  and spent 82 years wondering what  happened to her best friend  she talked about anna marie wrote about  her and brought her up every chance she  got  i don't know whatever happened to her  she probably died in the war  as the mission can now the odds were  against that mystery ever being solved  the odds that would have a happy ending  even less likely  but it would be worth watching to see  who betty's facetiming  on this park bench this is a story we  were very  lucky to tell that's tonight on the new  reality  robin looking forward to it thanks mike  and that is global national for this  saturday night i'm robin gill tonight  your canada is the aurora borealis in  alberta's mykolon lake  provincial park thanks for watching good  night  [Music]  you
 

